  "headline": "Government Opens 154,052 CPNS 2026 Positions and Sets SKD Thresholds",
  "seoTitle": "CPNS 2026 Registration Requirements and SKD Passing Grade",
  "metaDescription": "The government has launched the CPNS 2026 recruitment process for 154,052 positions, detailing SKD passing grades and official registration procedures.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The government has officially opened registration for 154,052 CPNS 2026 positions, with the application window closing on December 21.",
    "Minister of Administrative and Bureaucratic Reform Rini Widyantini has finalized the passing grade requirements for the Basic Competency Selection.",
    "Specific institutions, such as the BPKP, have announced dedicated allocations, while new policies allow certain veteran educators to apply."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian government has officially commenced the recruitment process for 154,052 civil servant positions, known as CPNS 2026, with the application period concluding on December 21. Head of the National Civil Service Agency (BKN) Zudan Arif Fakrulloh confirmed the selection timeline, while Minister of Administrative and Bureaucratic Reform Rini Widyantini established the necessary passing grade thresholds for the Basic Competency Selection (SKD). Various institutions are participating, including the BPKP, which has opened 2,007 positions to support national priorities. Additionally, updates include pathways for specific groups, such as educators over age 35, and simplified document requirements for applicants. Amid the recruitment rollout, discussions continue in the House of Representatives regarding potential future revisions to educational requirements for applicants. The process is managed centrally through the official SSCASN portal, where candidates must complete their registration and e-meterai document validation.",
